# VoidCode AI — Phase 2 data.
# The Codeforces corpus is NOT redistributable (see docs/DATA_SOURCES.md §1):
# the API publishes no open-data licence. Raw and derived data stay local.
/data/raw/
/data/warehouse/
*.jsonl.tmp
features/**/__pycache__/
scripts/memory_audit/out_*.jsonl
scripts/memory_audit/out_*.json

# VoidCode AI — Python tooling and Hive/Derby artifacts
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
derby.log
metastore_db/
/data/hive_warehouse/
.Rhistory
analysis/*.Rout
sql/**/*.out

# VoidCode AI — LLM corpora and model artifacts.
#
# Derived, large, and regenerable from the scripts in llm/scripts/. Keeping them
# out is also what makes the existing *.safetensors / *.bin rules coherent: the
# weights were already ignored, so committing a 10MB tokenizer.json beside them
# would ship an artifact that is useless without the file it accompanies.
#
# The corpora are the build output of the generation pipeline, not its source.
# Version the generator, not the ~70MB it emits.
llm/data/*.jsonl
# ...but NOT the eval gold sets. The rule above was written for the training corpora (51 MB across
# mode_*.jsonl and voidcode_training_data_v*.jsonl) and caught these with them. Gold sets are 48 KB
# total, hand-authored, and they ARE the definition of the metric -- an eval whose scenarios are
# untracked is not reproducible from a clone, and its numbers cannot be compared across machines.
# eval_debug_gold.jsonl had been untracked since it was written.
#
# The glob is `*gold*` and not `*_gold`, because the narrower form was written when every gold file
# ended in `_gold.jsonl` and then silently dropped `eval_debug_gold_extended.jsonl` -- the same
# failure a second time, in the fix for the first one. `test_every_gold_file_is_tracked_by_git`
# checks this by asking git rather than by reading this pattern.
!llm/data/eval_*gold*.jsonl
# Ignore the CONTENTS, not the directories themselves. Git cannot un-ignore a file inside an
# ignored directory, and these two dirs each hold an INCOMPLETE.md explaining that the weights
# live off-repo, how to regenerate them, and the transformers/llmcompressor version trap that
# left them empty for months. That explanation is documentation and belongs in git; the 5-15 GB
# of weights beside it does not. Ignoring the directory hid the explanation too.
llm/outputs/awq_model/*
!llm/outputs/awq_model/INCOMPLETE.md
llm/outputs/merged_model/*
!llm/outputs/merged_model/INCOMPLETE.md
*.bak

# Derived: cached out-of-fold IRT predictions from features/export_calibration.py.
# 9.5 MB, regenerable with --refit in ~10 minutes. The ARTIFACT (apps/api/data/
# calibration_map.json, 12 KB) is tracked on purpose; this is not.
.cache/

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Merged in from the RL training repo (voidcode-training) during consolidation.
# Paths are rewritten where that repo's `docs/` now lives at `docs/rl/`.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Root-level RL run output. Scoped with a leading slash on purpose: a bare
# `outputs/` would also swallow llm/outputs/, whose config and tokenizer files
# are tracked deliberately while only its weights are ignored above.
/outputs/
/checkpoints/

# The filtered DeepCoder sample: 885 MB, ~9x GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so a
# push would be rejected outright and the commit would bloat history permanently
# even after removal. Regenerate with scripts/adapt_deepcoder.py.
#
# data/deepcoder-band.json is deliberately NOT ignored: 373 KB, and it is the
# *result* of the paid A40 filter pass — it cannot be regenerated without
# renting the GPU again.
data/deepcoder-sample.json

# THE ANSWER KEY. data/catalogue.json carries reference solutions; publishing it
# destroys every benchmark that grades against it. The upstream training repo
# tracked it because that repo is private and its public mirror omits the file.
# This consolidated repo has no remote yet, so the file is ignored here rather
# than relying on that distinction holding. The file still exists on disk, so
# tests/test_differential.py runs normally — only committing is prevented.
# Remove this line ONLY if you are certain this repo will never be published.
data/catalogue.json

# Process detritus from detached pod/local runs, now under docs/rl/.
docs/rl/*.err
docs/rl/*.pid
bpr.log
bpr*.log
qwen7b-restore.log

# Pod run logs: hundreds of MB of generated-solution stdout (numpy array prints
# from graded candidates). The results live in the .json beside them; these are
# raw noise. A single-level `docs/*.log` nearly let a 164 MB and a 350 MB file in,
# so this is the recursive form.
docs/**/*.log

# Local copies of pod artefacts (adapters, tokenizers). The volume dies with the pod, so these
# are pulled off it for safekeeping -- but weights stay out of git, same as the *.safetensors rule.
artifacts/

# Desktop app build output and vendored runtime. `desktop/vendor/` holds Pyodide wheels fetched by
# `npm run vendor:pyodide`; electron-builder copies it as an extraResource at package time.
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/out/
desktop/vendor/
desktop/dist/
desktop/renderer/node_modules/
desktop/renderer/.next/
desktop/renderer/out/
